generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick 3 distinct colors for bg, lattice, marker.
    2. Choose cell_size in {3, 4}, num_h_lines in [3,4], num_v_lines in [4,5].
    3. Choose hole rectangle span (1-2 steps in rows, 1-2 steps in cols); pick which pair of lattice row/col indices form the 4 hole corners.
    4. Build the full grid — place lattice lines at regular intervals starting at offset=cell_size, fill cells with bg.
    5. Set exactly the 4 intersection pixels (hole corners) to bg instead of lattice_color.
    6. Scatter marker pixels randomly into cell interiors (density ~10-20% of cell area).
    7. Verify grid dimensions are 17-22 in each direction; pad/trim trailing cell strip if needed (rows/cols after last line can be 0 to cell_size).
    8. Output = inclusive crop inp[r0:r1+1, c0:c1+1] where (r0,c0)/(r1,c1) are hole positions.
